// Regression: a tuplet in ONE voice must not break another voice's beaming.
// Voice 1 has a quarter-note triplet (its "3" bracket sits above); voice 2 has
// eight straight eighths that must beam 4+4 (two half-measure groups), below,
// stems down. Auto-beaming breaks at a tuplet boundary, but only within the
// tuplet's OWN voice — the boundary index is voice-local. Before the fix the
// detector shared score.TupletBrackets across every voice, so voice 1's triplet
// end-index split voice 2's first group into [e' f'] + two stray flags, matching
// LilyPond only if you squint. Now tuplets carry a VoiceIndex and the detector
// filters by it. LILYPOND-REF: lily/auto-beam-engraver.cc — beaming is per Voice.
octave absolute
title "Multi-voice tuplet + beams"
part mel { clef treble }
section S {
  mel {
    voice { tuplet 3/2 { c''4 c'' c'' } c''2 | }
    voice { e'8 f' g' a' b' a' g' f' | }
  }
}
structure { S }
score "multivoice-tuplet-beams" { staff mel }
